  "title": "12 mm magnetic buzzer",
  "summary": "Externally driven 12 mm magnetic transducer, Same Sky CEM-1203(42). The coil is 42 ohm and the pins, marked + and -, are 6.5 mm apart. `hz` is the frequency of the square wave driving it, and 0 while that wave is absent. The sheet's operating voltage is 3 V to 5 V peak. A drive outside that still sounds, quieter, and the run warns. A Nano pin wired straight across the coil draws more than the pin's 40 mA, so the run warns. Drive it from 5 V through a transistor.",
